Dmb%wam.umd.edu@uunet.uu.net (David M. Baggett) writes:
>
>Although it's not a bug per se, I would say that being able to get
>trapped by your pet(s) is a bad "feature".  A recent example (maybe
>it's in the spoiler file?) was the following:
>
>	1) You walk down a dead end corridor.
>	2) Pet follows into corridor behind you.
>	3) Hill orc follows pet into corridor.
>	4) Pet kills Hill Orc; corpse now in corridor.
>	5) Hill Orc has a cursed item; pet won't cross item.
>	6) You are trapped unless your pet dies (assuming you
>	   can't teleport).
>
>I encountered a similar problem....

I've always wanted to  be able to urge my pet on somewhere.  With
real pets you can naturally shove them gently with your hand, or,
if need be, your foot.  It would be silly, though, to expect the
dev team to develop an "urge on" command.   Verbal commands are a
bit much, too.  Kicking now simply has the effect of injuring the
pet.  If it also had the effect of impelling the pet to move away
a few feet in the direction of the kick - even over a cursed  item -
we might have our ticket for rare curcumstances such as those men-
tioned above.  I would naturally feel bad about kicking a pet.  I
would feel even worse, however, about having to kill it just to go
back out of a corridor...

-Richard


